#
# Code owners for Gable. GitHub requests a review from the matching owner
# whenever a pull request touches one of these paths.
#
# !! PLACEHOLDER TEAMS !!
# The handles below do NOT exist yet. Before opening the repo to outside
# contributors a maintainer must:
#   1. Create the teams under the @FutureBuildAIinc organisation (Settings ->
#      Teams). Suggested: maintainers, backend, frontend, docs, infra, legal.
#   2. Give each team at least *write* access to this repository — GitHub
#      silently ignores CODEOWNERS entries for teams without write access, so a
#      typo or a missing grant looks exactly like "nothing happened".
#   3. Replace every handle here with the real one, or collapse them all to
#      @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers if the split is premature.
#   4. Enable "Require review from Code Owners" in the branch protection rules
#      for `main` and `staging`.
#
# Syntax: last matching pattern wins, so the specific overrides at the bottom
# take precedence over the catch-all at the top.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default owner for everything not matched below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                           @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Components (mirrors LICENSE-MAP.md)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/backend/                   @FutureBuildAIinc/backend
/app/                       @FutureBuildAIinc/frontend
/docs/                      @FutureBuildAIinc/docs

# The connector seam is the third-party integration boundary and is licensed
# differently (Connector, not Commons) — changes here need maintainer eyes.
/backend/pkg/apps/          @FutureBuildAIinc/backend @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers

# Database migrations are append-only and irreversible in production.
/backend/migrations/        @FutureBuildAIinc/backend @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CI / release plumbing
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.github/                   @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers
/.do/                       @FutureBuildAIinc/infra
/docker-compose.yml         @FutureBuildAIinc/infra
/Makefile                   @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers
/backend/Dockerfile         @FutureBuildAIinc/infra
/app/Dockerfile             @FutureBuildAIinc/infra

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Licensing and legal — maintainer approval always required.
# These files define what the project *is* legally; a bad merge here is far
# more expensive to unwind than a bad merge in application code.
#
# There is deliberately no /brand/ rule: this repository ships no logo or
# wordmark files. The marks live in the separate `brand` repository, together
# with the trademark policy that governs them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/LICENSE                    @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers @FutureBuildAIinc/legal
/LICENSE-MAP.md             @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers @FutureBuildAIinc/legal
/LICENSES/                  @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers @FutureBuildAIinc/legal
/REUSE.toml                 @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers @FutureBuildAIinc/legal
/NOTICE                     @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers @FutureBuildAIinc/legal
/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md     @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers @FutureBuildAIinc/legal
/SECURITY.md                @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md         @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers
/CONTRIBUTING.md            @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers
